{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/reviews/id196756505"}, "name":{"label":"SnailMech"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2024-07-24T17:30:36-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"2024.7.2"}, "id":{"label":"11531325543"}, "title":{"label":"Well designed, just works!"}, "content":{"label":"Stays out of your way in the best way possible. Little details like rewinding slightly after a pause are barely noticeable but make the experience much better! \nSupport indie devs!", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/review?id=888422857&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/reviews/id22163201"}, "name":{"label":"emonxie"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2024-07-24T13:20:00-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"3"}, "im:version":{"label":"2024.7.2"}, "id":{"label":"11530725908"}, "title":{"label":"Poor UX - update has made the app harder to manage"}, "content":{"label":"I pay for the full featured app because I valued the content management controls it used to have. Now it’s a giant, time wasting pain in the backside to try to manage how many episodes for a given podcast I’d like to cache / download, and despite setting a playlist to feature new episodes first I’m instead getting stacks of five episodes or more per podcast in the playlist, meaning instead of getting whatever has dropped on the day, a key thing for news related podcasts, I’m getting old content from sometimes a month ago, stuff that should’ve been purged / deleted to make room for more recent content. This causes the app’s footprint to get huge on the phone as well as serving up out of date content in my playlist. I miss the old controls, where I could easily set limits to how many episodes of a podcast would download with the reliable expectation that old episodes would be deleted to make room for new ones, regardless whether I’d listened to them or not. I also missed that my podcast download rules didn’t apply to things I’d manually downloaded, as that also appears to be getting inconsistently applied, as I’ve had manually downloaded content disappear such that I have to redownload it later when I get around to listening to it. Not sure who the UX updates were intended to serve, definitely wasn’t me. I would love to have some macro controls back such as globally controlling how many episodes might download generally and / or within a playlist, and a way to organize playlists by date to prevent the weird stacking happening now.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/review?id=888422857&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
